    {
      "id": "claim_4ce72e88d64d4bcaa63069a33af7e3ba",
      "statement": "The tool-builder agent's canonical Voyager flow is: write_file the implementation, read_file to re-read it, write_file the pytest suite, run_bash to run pytest, then register_tool_file to commit it to tool_registry/ and registry.yaml.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agents/tool-builder/agent.yaml#L48-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:25d4ad8687d7200261f4a2031be4cf71bd8df0ad7f490de1f43ba428ba296f2f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/TOOL-REGISTRY.md#L28-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:337b911d9e692f4276f4c8ad06abbb75499a6e0dcaf082bd937426c3d2f7a16a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b75c93a28b6b45828d832fc8367ab9f5",
      "statement": "The tool-builder spec enforces the flow with must/must_not guardrails: must re-read the implementation before writing tests, must run pytest before registering, must register only after tests pass, must finish with the exact phrase 'TOOL REGISTERED'; must_not register with failing tests and must_not claim pytest passed without executing run_bash.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agents/tool-builder/agent.yaml#L48-L56",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:25d4ad8687d7200261f4a2031be4cf71bd8df0ad7f490de1f43ba428ba296f2f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c02379d56e65457aa78c33d9195628ea",
      "statement": "The engine's must-compliance check (AgentRuntime._missing_must_files) deterministically verifies that filename-shaped quoted terms in guardrails.must rules exist on disk in AGENT_WORKDIR before a run is considered compliant, complementing the LLM judge.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/runtime/engine.py#L353-L354",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:598d0ab2782d66e4b66d326c318e0d87af4296376e41f27c0cd17bc795806ac7:"
