    },
    {
      "id": "claim_99595b7ac8fe4adc83945e70d040da6e",
      "statement": "write_file and read_file resolve relative paths against AGENT_WORKDIR; write_file creates parent directories on demand; read_file truncates output at 8000 characters with a truncation marker.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/tools/write_file.py#L7-L32",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b496d24c6ee4391cd6e95adb6eb38fa61e7d7bcff0880b15eab082c483aeb935:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_051e88c406c346f3a69a299f41e24d3e",
      "statement": "run_bash executes commands in AGENT_WORKDIR with a destructive-command regex blocklist, a BASH_TIMEOUT (default 1800 s) that kills the process on expiry, and captures output to a temporary file (not a pipe) truncated to 4000 characters; the temp-file design is a deliberate fix so backgrounded child processes cannot hold the pipe open past the timeout.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/tools/run_bash.py#L11-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:41f24a9feb8ee10db5d79737d65802c12e0b4f1b0f6cca8872c4cef3b192357a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_da0275158f9242d3a23ae31bf69b6b3f",
      "statement": "register_tool_file validates in order: (1) source file exists (resolved against AGENT_WORKDIR, absolute paths pass through); (2) ast.parse succeeds (SyntaxError reported); (3) the module imports cleanly as a fresh module under synthetic key _agentforge_validate_<tool_name> via importlib.util.spec_from_file_location/exec_module; (4) getattr(module, function_name) returns a callable. Any failure returns {'success': false, 'error': '<reason>'} without touching the registry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/tools/register_tool_file.py#L21-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0bfb2ea72a8260e6d6dded51266c0b2bfdfeaff2dca3e443211b58411f885c97:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f23482d73e4d4296b73f696acfccf838",
      "statement": "On success, register_tool_file copies the source to tool_registry/<tool_name>.py via shutil.copy2, rewrites tool_registry/registry.yaml by removing any existing entry with the same tool_name then appending a new one (fields: name, file, function, description, input_schema, created_by, registered_at ISO-8601 UTC), and registers the loaded function in the live _ToolRegistry via register_tool so the tool is callable in the current process without a restart.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/tools/register_tool_file.py#L75-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49c9262d6335540872ebc8820541a9c22874e619e5cc4da06ecec5a71c024b04:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_59b7afbb91e94e73a0826c61552b1790",
      "statement": "Re-registering a tool with the same tool_name silently overwrites the previous version: the copy step replaces tool_registry/<tool_name>.py and the manifest rewrite removes the old entry, so there is no version history in registry.yaml.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/TOOL-REGISTRY.md#L191-L196",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a1000862941c8db2840871bd5403bf621a51e3dfe92ef6c771b75259ec3b47f1:"
